  "question": {
    "text": "A simple pendulum, consisting of a small ball of mass $m$ attached to a massless string hanging vertically from the ceiling, is oscillating with an amplitude such that $T_{\\max }=2 T_{\\min }$ where $T_{\\max }$ and $T_{\\min }$ are the maximum and minimum tension in the string respectively. The value of maximum tension $\\mathrm{T}_{\\max }$ in the string is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3 m g}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{mg}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3 m g}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$3 \\mathrm{mg}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0006_8ad046b0280a.png\"><br>\r\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\min }=m g \\cos \\theta$\r\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\max }=\\mathrm{mg}+\\frac{\\mathrm{mv}^{2}}{\\mathrm{I}}=\\mathrm{mg}+\\frac{\\mathrm{mv}^{2}}{\\mathrm{I}}$\r\n$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{mv}^{2}=\\mathrm{mgl}(1-\\cos \\theta)$\r\n$\\mathrm{T}_{\\max }=2 \\mathrm{~T}_{\\min }$\r\n$\\mathrm{mg}+\\frac{\\mathrm{mv}^{2}}{\\mathrm{I}}=2 \\mathrm{mg} \\cos \\theta$\r\n$\\therefore \\cos \\theta=\\frac{3}{4}$\r\n$\\mathrm{v}^{2}=2 \\mathrm{gl}\\left(1-\\frac{3}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\mathrm{gl}}{2}$\r\n$\\mathrm{~T}_{\\max }=\\mathrm{mg}+\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{I}} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{l}}{2}=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{mg}}{2}$"
  }
}